  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA distributed value fell 4.1% over 30D:</strong> On-chain RWA distributed value at $14.25B (4.1% lower over 30D). Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/11/04/morgan-stanley-says-it-is-among-the-first-banks-to-put-u-s-stocks-and-treasuries-on-a-blockchain\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Morgan Stanley says it is among the first banks to tokenize real world assets</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/converge/tradfi-and-fintech/soci-t-g-n-rale-accepts-10-million-in-dtcc-tokenized-treasuries-as-collateral\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Soci\u00e9t\u00e9 G\u00e9n\u00e9rale Accepts $10 Million in DTCC-Tokenized Treasuries as Collateral</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Institutional commitments are still a leading share signal:</strong> Bank and asset-manager distribution deals often shift platform and network leadership before headline RWA totals fully catch up. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/business/2026-11-04-bitgo-launches-institutional-trading-and-financial-solutions-business-led-by-former-nydig-executive-432646\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BitGo launches institutional trading and financial solutions business led by former NYDIG executive</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/11/04/wall-street-cuts-bitcoin-miner-price-targets-after-democrats-texas-win-threatens-ai-data-center-boom\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Wall Street rethinks AI data center boom as Texas election raises new risks</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
